    "title": "Space to breathe - NewsBreak",
    "text": "1 days ago On July 6, 2026, the City of Carlsbad broke ground on its 43rd park for our fair city, the Veterans Memorial Park. Located off Faraday Avenue near Canon Road, Veterans Memorial Park will cover 94 acres in total, with 53 of those acres being dedicated as protected open-space habitat. This will be a great addition to Carlsbad. This community asset will include a large Veterans Memorial Plaza with memorial art, multiple picnic areas, large playgrounds, a bike park, trails, viewpoints, and more. Read full article",
